# `std::collections::lru_cache` — Bounded Doubly-Linked LRU Cache (`LruCache`)

## 1. Design Intent & Rust `lru::LruCache` Comparison

In Rust's `lru` crate, maintaining a bounded-capacity cache with $O(1)$ MRU promotion and LRU eviction requires a doubly-linked list cross-referenced with a table via raw pointers (`NonNull<LruEntry<K, V>>`) and dozens of `unsafe` blocks to bypass the borrow checker's single-mutable-alias restriction.

In Jenny's `std::collections::lru_cache`, `LruCache` composes `std::mem::raw_buf::RawBuf` (`self.buf.cap == self.capacity * 5`, storing `[active, key, val, prev, next]` per slot) with machine-checked invariants:
- `invariant self.capacity >= 1 && self.capacity <= 65536`
- `invariant self.len >= 0 && self.len <= self.capacity`
- `invariant self.buf.cap == self.capacity * 5`
- `invariant self.hits >= 0 && self.misses >= 0 && self.evictions >= 0`
- `get_promote(mut self, key)` promotes the accessed entry to the MRU `head` and increments `hits` (`ensures self.hits == old(self.hits) + 1 && self.mru_key == key`).
- `put(mut self, key, val)` inserts or updates `key`, evicting the LRU `tail` entry when `self.len == self.capacity` (`ensures self.mru_key == key`).

## 2. Formal Interface & Contracts

```jenny
module std_collections_lru_cache

import std::mem::raw_buf

pub enum LruError {
    KeyNotFound,
    InvalidCapacity,
}

pub struct LruCache {
    buf: RawBuf,
    capacity: i64,
    len: i64 = 0,
    head: i64 = -1,
    tail: i64 = -1,
    mru_key: i64 = 0,
    hits: i64 = 0,
    misses: i64 = 0,
    evictions: i64 = 0,

    invariant self.capacity >= 1 && self.capacity <= 65536
    invariant self.len >= 0 && self.len <= self.capacity
    invariant (self.buf.cap == 0 && self.len == 0) || (self.buf.cap == self.capacity * 5)
    invariant self.hits >= 0 && self.misses >= 0 && self.evictions >= 0
}

impl LruCache {
    pub fn new(capacity: i64) -> LruCache ! LruError
        effects [AllocNative]
        requires capacity >= 1 && capacity <= 65536 else LruError.InvalidCapacity
        ensures result.capacity == capacity && result.len == 0 && result.hits == 0 && result.evictions == 0

    pub fn len(self) -> i64
        effects []
        ensures result == self.len

    pub fn promote_slot(mut self, slot: i64) -> i64 ! LruError
        effects [Mutate]
        requires slot >= 0 && slot < self.len else LruError.KeyNotFound
        ensures self.head == slot && self.len == old(self.len)

    pub fn put(mut self, key: i64, val: i64) -> i64 ! LruError
        effects [Mutate]
        ensures self.len >= 1 && self.len <= self.capacity && self.mru_key == key

    pub fn get_promote(mut self, key: i64) -> i64 ! LruError
        effects [Mutate]
        requires self.len > 0 else LruError.KeyNotFound
        ensures self.hits == old(self.hits) + 1 && self.mru_key == key

    pub fn peek(self, key: i64) -> i64 ! LruError
        effects []
        requires self.len > 0 else LruError.KeyNotFound

    pub fn drop_cache(mut self) -> i64
        effects [Mutate]
        ensures self.len == 0 && self.buf.cap == 0
}

@example("EX-STD-LRU-01: LruCache MRU promotion, bounded LRU tail eviction, and zero-leak drop") {
    var cache = LruCache.new(3)!
    cache.put(10, 100)!
    cache.put(20, 200)!
    cache.put(30, 300)!
    assert(cache.len() == 3)
    assert(cache.mru_key == 30)
    val v10 = cache.get_promote(10)!
    assert(v10 == 100)
    assert(cache.mru_key == 10)
    assert(cache.hits == 1)
    cache.put(40, 400)!
    assert(cache.len() == 3)
    assert(cache.evictions == 1)
    assert(cache.mru_key == 40)
    val evicted = cache.peek(20)
    assert(evicted is Err(LruError.KeyNotFound))
    assert(cache.peek(10)! == 100)
    assert(cache.peek(30)! == 300)
    assert(cache.peek(40)! == 400)
    cache.drop_cache()
    assert(active_native_boxes() == 0)
}

@example("EX-STD-LRU-02: LruCache rejects invalid capacity and missing key lookup") {
    val bad_cap = LruCache.new(0)
    assert(bad_cap is Err(LruError.InvalidCapacity))
    var cache = LruCache.new(2)!
    val e1 = cache.get_promote(99)
    assert(e1 is Err(LruError.KeyNotFound))
    cache.drop_cache()
    assert(active_native_boxes() == 0)
}
```
